      "retired_reason": "Re-baselined: the mutation sampler moved from random.gauss (Box-Muller over the platform-dependent math.cos) to the Marsaglia polar method, so genetics reproduce across machines. The polar method consumes a variable number of RNG draws where gauss consumes exactly two, which reshuffles every downstream random decision and moves scores; this is an expected consequence of the fix, not a performance change. Values taken from CI's own run (bench.yml run 30477908610, commit on fix/platform-independent-mutation-sampler) rather than a local re-run, per the cross-platform divergence this very change addresses. config_hash unchanged - code behaviour only. poker/ladder_20k and soccer/ladder_5k still reproduce exactly and are untouched.",
